@DanTheManShelley [LRH], Etiqueta de servidor: LRHLRHAgree with @dihensoeur, I wouldn't allow it as it's no longer their turn and they want to change the board state by more than one action.  In a casual game, yeah you probably would allow it.  Something I'm trying to drum into my locals is calling lore guides when someone wants to do a take back. As players are allowing take backs with multiple steps to happen which is no bueno.Mallow_Of_MarsS2 DLC BEL — 26/6/26, 11:34viernes, 26 de junio de 2026, 11:34I'm going to nitpick a bit but how would moving 1 character to a location be changing the board state by more than 1 action. 

I would be hesitant to say yes to that change immediately, but I don't think it's an unreasonable request to take back you passing your turn if your opponent is still in his ready phase , just to move 1 character to a location. 

But as always, you have to judge these on a game to game basis and try to be as consistent as possible.

@GooglyGlimmers [LRH], Etiqueta de servidor: LRHLRHWe will find out the rules when the rules are updated.  I would anticipate the worst as far as inheriting states like ready/exerted.  I would anticipate that everything other than states will be inherited completely. Effects, damage, etc.  I would anticipate that inheriting multiple copies of a keyword ability hasn’t been deeply considered and will not be known immediately.kleptokatt (MJ - IN) [LRH], Etiqueta de servidor: LRHLRHLore Guide — 30/6/26, 0:31martes, 30 de junio de 2026, 0:31With respect to your latter point, inheriting multiple copies of a keyword, wouldn't this follow the precedent of double-application from effects and keywords already printed on a card?
For instance, Ranger Plane giving Support to a character that already has the support keyword.  You don't get double support.

For curiosity's sake, are there any cards currently that pass their keywords to the card(s) on top of them?  None come to mind, but each set they add takes up more of my RAM, and I'm about at my limit.  And thanks to NVidia, RAM is stupid expensive right now.

